{"title":"1999 IMO Problems/Problem 2","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(elegant)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (elegant)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Resources\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Resources</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_IMO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>(<i>Marcin Kuczma, Poland</i>)\nLet <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/2/72287b09043ed45b372a517d764e12d07aff8071.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\geq 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"14\" /> be a fixed integer.\n</p>\n<ul><li>(a) Find the least constant <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> such that for all nonnegative real numbers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/2/192b4c547e043d62cf3d22f0965252a5c8651a31.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_1, \\dots, x_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"76\" height=\"11\" />,</li></ul>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/0/5808d2668e5523b39963ef94f3ca6ad8f6b20a89.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sum_{1\\leq i&lt;j \\leq n} x_ix_j (x_i^2 + x_j^2) \\leq C \\left( \\sum_{i=1}^n x_i \\right)^4.\\]\" width=\"292\" height=\"57\" />\n</p>\n<ul><li>(b) Determine when equality occurs for this value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />.</li></ul>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_IMO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/4/ee4ac5bf0207347d74b9527a74d2d90124e55e7a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C=1/8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"65\" height=\"18\" />, and equality holds exactly when two of the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/b/67bc6daa9d6b964201d6cef60cbeb1ac5fd26ead.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"15\" height=\"10\" /> are equal to each other and all the other <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/b/67bc6daa9d6b964201d6cef60cbeb1ac5fd26ead.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"15\" height=\"10\" /> are zero.  We prove this by <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Induction\" title=\"Induction\">induction</a> on the number of nonzero <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/b/67bc6daa9d6b964201d6cef60cbeb1ac5fd26ead.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"15\" height=\"10\" />.\n</p><p>First, suppose that at most two of the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/b/67bc6daa9d6b964201d6cef60cbeb1ac5fd26ead.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"15\" height=\"10\" />, say <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/9/d891e80cc17277408da4e49e686269869441eb38.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"17\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/7/f4707250ff456bd3d80210854c1beadbe2e2b276.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"16\" height=\"10\" />, are nonzero.  Then the left-hand side of the desired inequality becomes <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/c/a8c917baccea0e104ab89608310e4f3b842943e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_a x_b (x_a^2 + x_b^2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"110\" height=\"21\" /> and the right-hand side becomes <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/c/5/1c56feb52ba3493a6ddacece7bebb49a1eda9dd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x_a + x_b)^4/8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"97\" height=\"19\" />.  By <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AM-GM\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"AM-GM\">AM-GM</a>,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/0/b80e80f2e548b93bc74d6b95b9d0f8f7a43ccd8f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} x_a x_b(x_a^2 + x_b^2) = 1/2 \\left[ \\sqrt{(2x_ax_b)(x_a^2 + x_b^2)} \\right]^2 &amp;\\le \\frac{1}{2} \\left( \\frac{x_a^2 + 2x_a x_b + x_b^2}{2} \\right)^2 \\\\ &amp;= (x_a + x_b)^2/8, \\end{align*}\" width=\"539\" height=\"72\" />\nwith equality exactly when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/f/82ff8779a42c80f99d7ad494cf66889dbe2e1710.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_a = x_b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"58\" height=\"10\" />, as desired.\n</p><p>Now, suppose that our statement holds when at most <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> of the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/b/67bc6daa9d6b964201d6cef60cbeb1ac5fd26ead.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"15\" height=\"10\" /> are equal to zero.  Suppose now that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/0/5/f05f085f774fc8ab50676b778b86a1f1d1114fc8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"16\" /> of the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/b/67bc6daa9d6b964201d6cef60cbeb1ac5fd26ead.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"15\" height=\"10\" /> are equal to zero, for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/e/19e4194d33d81c3dd5ac49c773335504c4a7a0d1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k\\ge 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"15\" />.  <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Without_loss_of_generality\" title=\"Without loss of generality\">Without loss of generality</a>, let these be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/b/9fb65b4eb7e5a5652b80dce4758c9d320b88a347.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_1 \\ge \\dotsb \\ge x_k \\ge x_{k+1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"163\" height=\"16\" />.\nWe define\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/a/c0a2eb8f294d1af9ee60479958588409f674c5fa.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[y_j = \\begin{cases} x_j, &amp; j \\notin \\{k, k+1\\} \\\\ x_k + x_{k+1}, &amp; j=k \\\\ 0, &amp; j=k+1 \\end{cases} ,\\]\" width=\"270\" height=\"74\" />\nand for convenience, we will denote <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/b/80b62f15e057a3326606e2bbf8a8a2bbf683f6b1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S= \\sum_{i=1}^{k-1} x_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -20px\" width=\"80\" height=\"51\" />.  We wish to show that by replacing the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/b/67bc6daa9d6b964201d6cef60cbeb1ac5fd26ead.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"15\" height=\"10\" /> with the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/6/6e6ceb79ebc4bf613298e0144eae25dd73de9be3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"13\" height=\"11\" />, we increase the left-hand side of the desired inequality without changing the right-hand side; and then to use the inductive hypothesis.\n</p><p>We note that\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/2/f12fbfc780140017daa90d4b87b83813fc1adcf7.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} \\sum_{1\\le i&lt; j \\le n} x_i x_j(x_i^2 + x_j^2) ={}&amp; \\sum_{1 \\le i&lt;j \\le k-1} x_i x_j(x_i^2 + x_j^2) + \\sum_{1 \\le i \\le k-1} \\left[ x_ix_k(x_i^2 + x_k^2) + x_ix_{k+1}(x_i^2 + x_{k+1}^2) \\right] \\\\ &amp; + x_k x_{k+1}(x_k^2 + x_{k+1}^2) \\\\ ={}&amp; \\sum_{1 \\le i&lt;j \\le k-1} x_i x_j(x_i^2 + x_j^2) + \\sum_{i=1}^{k-1} x_i^3 (x_k + x_{k+1}) + S(x_k^3 + x_{k+1}^3) \\\\ &amp;+ x_k^3 x_{k+1} + x_k x_{k+1}^3 \\end{align*}\" width=\"736\" height=\"161\" />\nIf we replace <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/9/c49756d8db18483c6fb499506c6edf6f24880a49.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S(x_k^3 + x_{k+1}^3) + x_k^3 x_{k+1} + x_k x_{k+1}^3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"252\" height=\"21\" /> becomes\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/3/e33756a2055481332ea77b67c3151c5a402a7c6c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[S(x_k + x_{k+1})^3 = S(x_k + x_{k+1})^3 + 3S(x_k^2 x_{k+1} + x_k x_{k+1}^2),\\]\" width=\"435\" height=\"21\" />\nbut none of the other terms change.  Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26e6f4d00f812b0b3aab441e19cf210f1589a2f6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3S &gt; S \\ge a_1 \\ge a_k, a_{k+1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"181\" height=\"16\" />, it follows that we have strictly increased the right-hand side of the equation, i.e.,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/4/854685ed0914854d28a0675dcf45844e90084019.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sum_{1 \\le i&lt;j \\le n} x_i x_j (x_i^2 + x_j^2) &lt; \\sum_{1 \\le i&lt;j \\le n} y_i y_j (y_i^2 + y_j^2) .\\]\" width=\"352\" height=\"40\" />\nBy inductive hypothesis,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/6/b96684493ffe843f7e8933d1a9b07d678adfd758.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sum_{1\\le i&lt;j \\le n} y_i y_j (y_i^2 +y_j^2) \\le \\left( \\sum_{i=1}^n y_i \\right)^4 / 8 ,\\]\" width=\"287\" height=\"57\" />\nand by our choice of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/6/6e6ceb79ebc4bf613298e0144eae25dd73de9be3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"13\" height=\"11\" />,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/e/5de35faf49d603580ebda3c9e52c2bcd3d29742b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\left( \\sum_{i=1}^n y_i \\right)^4/8 = \\left( \\sum_{i=1}^n x_i \\right)^4/8 .\\]\" width=\"225\" height=\"56\" />\nHence the problem's inequality holds by induction, and is strict when there are more than two nonzero <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/b/67bc6daa9d6b964201d6cef60cbeb1ac5fd26ead.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"15\" height=\"10\" />, as desired.  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/b/3bbb9e25e5be095e317771a9c5d00877ee9c8012.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\blacksquare$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28elegant.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(elegant)\">Solution 2 (elegant)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_IMO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (elegant)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>I claim that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/9/39952622152bf6ce5f4960ee9e5796d1671e8c42.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C=\\frac{1}{8}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"50\" height=\"37\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/9/379980a40136ef1d85f6bc27e61c3e225a1262a5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_2=\\sum_{i=1}^nx_i^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -20px\" width=\"88\" height=\"48\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/c/7/1c7f17704b0b944b634e977d50940bd8a073445e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_2=\\sum_{1\\leq i&lt;j\\leq n}x_ix_j$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"134\" height=\"40\" />. Note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/6/c062990a221ca258a81d203e8ed1c33ad133d069.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sum_{1\\leq i&lt;j\\leq n}x_ix_j\\left(x_i^2+x_j^2\\right)\\leq\\sum_{1\\leq i&lt;j\\leq n}x_ix_jP_2=P_2S_2=\\frac{\\left(2\\sqrt{P_2\\cdot2S_2}\\right)^2}{8}\\leq\\frac{\\left(P_2+2S_2\\right)^2}{8}=\\frac{1}{8}\\left(\\sum_{i=1}^nx_i\\right)^4.\\]\" width=\"750\" height=\"57\" /> Equality holds in the first ineq when all but two of the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/b/67bc6daa9d6b964201d6cef60cbeb1ac5fd26ead.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"15\" height=\"10\" /> are zero, and this reduces to the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/b/6cb7ae00764b56ee2adf59e78a1ffde9685b80db.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" /> case which we can easily show to be equivalent to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/8/1/68168f31d69a59fa53164de932f876210da61e62.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left(x_1-x_2\\right)^4\\geq0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"112\" height=\"21\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/1/271696787bb2c79a7b3166276701259a23a5a710.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_1=x_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"58\" height=\"10\" />. That is, equality holds when two <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/b/67bc6daa9d6b964201d6cef60cbeb1ac5fd26ead.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"15\" height=\"10\" /> are the same and the rest are zero.\n</p><p>Q.E.D.\n</p><p><i>Alternate solutions are always welcome. If you have a different, elegant solution to this problem, please <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=1999_IMO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit\">add it</a> to this page.</i>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Resources\">Resources</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_IMO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Resources\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_IMO_Problems\" title=\"1999 IMO Problems\">1999 IMO Problems</a></li>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.mathlinks.ro/Forum/viewtopic.php?p=131846#p131846\">Discussion on AoPS/MathLinks</a></li></ul>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_IMO\" title=\"1999 IMO\">1999 IMO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_IMO_Problems\" title=\"1999 IMO Problems\">Problems</a></b>) • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c3222\">Resources</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_IMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1999 IMO Problems/Problem 1\">Problem 1</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"34%\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_IMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1999 IMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_IMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1999 IMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_IMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1999 IMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_IMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1999 IMO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_IMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1999 IMO Problems/Problem 6\">6</a>\n</td>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_IMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1999 IMO Problems/Problem 3\">Problem 3</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=IMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"IMO Problems and Solutions\"> All IMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017005250\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.031 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.053 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 283/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1238/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 44/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 4/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 9633/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   14.518      1 -total\n 51.67%    7.502      1 Template:Alternate_solutions\n 47.39%    6.880      1 Template:IMO_box\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:6097:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017005250 and revision id 204271. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}